        'The core insight: your app already has a build pipeline (Vite) that understands SFCs, TS, aliases, and plugins. Jest required a SECOND pipeline (babel-jest/ts-jest, CJS, moduleNameMapper duplicating aliases) that drifted from reality. Vitest runs tests through the same transforms as dev — what runs in tests is what ships.',
        'Native ESM first: no CJS interop hacks, top-level await works, and module mocking is implemented against the ESM module graph. Jest predates stable ESM and still wrestles with it.',
        'Execution model: a pool of worker threads/processes; each test FILE runs isolated with a fresh module registry, files run in parallel. test.concurrent parallelizes within a file. Watch mode reruns only the dependency-affected files using Vite\'s module graph — HMR-grade feedback.',
        'Config: a single vitest.config.ts (or a test block in vite.config.ts): environment ("node" | "jsdom" | "happy-dom"), globals (opt-in describe/it/expect without imports), setupFiles (jest-dom matchers, MSW server lifecycle), coverage provider (v8 default, istanbul optional).',
